  "nl_text": "The database named rschema_0026 contains seven tables, each representing a different entity or relationship in the system. The Textile table stores information about the textiles produced by the company, including their name, price, production date, and type. The Department table contains information about the different departments within the company, including their contact information, department name, and manager. The Inventory table tracks the quantity of textiles in stock and the date they were stocked in. The Employee table contains information about the employees within the company, including their department, name, gender, phone number, position, and employee ID. The Production_Relationship table tracks the production process, including the producer, production time, and quantity produced. The Sales_Relationship table tracks the sales process, including the customer, quantity sold, sales personnel, and sales time. The Performance_Evaluation table contains information about the performance of each employee, including their evaluation date, performance ID, score, and employee ID. Foreign keys are used to establish relationships between tables, ensuring data consistency and integrity.",
  "gold_question": "A textile enterprise needs to manage the production, inventory, and sales of textiles. Each textile has information such as name, type, production date, and price. The enterprise has multiple departments, and each department has a name, manager, and contact information. Employee management includes employee ID, name, gender, phone, and position. For each production, the system needs to record the produced product, quantity, producer, and production time. For inventory management, the system should record the products in stock, quantity, and stock-in time. For sales, the system should record the products sold, quantity, sales personnel, customer, and sales time. The system should also support performance evaluation for each department. The performance evaluation should record the evaluation date and performance score of each employee.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0026.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0026\nCREATE TABLE `textile` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `production_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `type` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `department` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_info` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `manager` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `inventory` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `textile_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `stocked_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `inventory_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`textile_id`) REFERENCES `textile` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `employee` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `department_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `gender` char(1) NOT NULL,\n  `phone_number` varchar(15) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `position` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `employee_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`department_id`) REFERENCES `department` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `production_relationship` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `producer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `production_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_produced` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `sales_relationship` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `customer` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `quantity_sold` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_personnel` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `performance_evaluation` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `employee_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `evaluation_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `performance_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `score` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `performance_evaluation_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employee_id`) REFERENCES `employee` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
